Customer Complaints (RCA) – Data Preparation & KPI Development Summary
1. Objective
The objective of this phase was to prepare a clean, consistent dataset from the raw consumer complaints data and to define a set of Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) that will support future analysis and reporting.

2. Data Cleaning and Transformation
A structured data cleaning process was applied to ensure data quality and usability:
•	Data Type Standardization
o	Converted key fields such as complaint_id and zip_code into numeric formats.
o	Standardized date fields (date_received, date_sent_to_company) into proper DATE data types.
•	Date Format Normalization
o	Resolved inconsistencies between UK (dd/MM/yyyy) and US (MM/dd/yyyy) formats.
o	Implemented conditional logic using TRY_CONVERT to correctly parse ambiguous dates.
o	Ensured all date fields are reliable for time-based calculations.
•	Text Cleaning
o	Removed leading and trailing spaces using LTRIM and RTRIM.
o	Replaced NULL or missing values with standardized labels such as 'Unknown'.
•	Categorical Standardization
o	Normalized fields such as:
	subproduct
	timely_response
	consumer_disputed
o	Grouped inconsistent labels into consistent categories (e.g., “Other debt” → “Debt”).

3. Derived Fields Creation
Additional fields were created to support KPI calculations:
•	Year Extracted
o	year_received derived from date_received.
•	Response Time
o	Calculated using:
DATEDIFF(day, date_received, date_sent_to_company)
o	Includes logic to handle invalid cases (e.g., negative durations).
•	Data Quality Flags
o	Flag created to identify invalid timelines where response dates precede received dates.

4. View Creation
A clean, reusable SQL view was created:
•	Combines all transformations into a single structured dataset.
•	Serves as the single source of truth for reporting and KPI calculations.
•	Ensures consistency across all downstream queries and dashboards.
•	Avoids modifying the original raw dataset.
